From 913fdc4352177835c60cc32d8b2da903a0d50a3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 19:52:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.5.14: session-end diagnostics, 10 s silence
 notice, wall clock in netlat, version in the boot line, KEYS OFF in the GBA
 window title, GBA frame copied before crossing threads

- gba_detect: 'session-end kind=peer-lost|local-stop reason=...',
  'stop-request local|server', 'player-left pid=' (server side) and
  'link-silent ms=' lines, each stamped with the local wall clock; 'netlat'
  lines carry wall=; the boot cpu line carries orrelink=<version>.
- WaitOnRemote: one yellow OSD line after 10 s without data from the other
  side (the session ends at 20 s), so a still screen is never silent.
- GBAWidget title shows 'KEYS OFF: click the game or a GBA window' while
  Background Input is off and no game window is active.
- GBAHost::FrameEnded copies the core's frame before queueing it to the UI
  thread; the span could outlive the buffer at a stop.
- XDNetplay::VERSION 1.5.14.
